            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all six changed paths. storedRef in engine/review/evidence.go refactors ResultRef and adds ExemptionRef while keeping the same path-shape validation: the results-dir prefix is required, exactly two segments are allowed, CheckFeature is applied, and a per-kind name check runs. Traversal, absolute paths, backslashes, hidden or dotted features and extra segments are still refused before any file is read.",
              "CheckExemptionName in engine/review/names.go reuses the existing stem helper with exemptionSuffix, so it enforces the strict 12-hex head and canonical number. Result and verdict names do not pass the exemption check, and exemption names do not pass the result check, as exercised by the added tests.",
              "ErrEvidenceMissing message is split so RequiredEvidence appends the record kind. The text for a review-report is unchanged, and no security-relevant behavior changes.",
              "No secrets, new dependencies, unsafe input handling, or authorization changes are introduced. The tests are additive and include negative path-traversal cases."
            ]
          }
        }
