            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "The ResultRef refactor into storedRef keeps the original ordering: prefix and segment shape check, then CheckFeature, then the name check. It also keeps the same ErrEvidenceRef wrapping. The only change for results is that the result-ref test list gains an exempt.json case, which is still refused.",
              "ErrEvidenceMissing now carries only 'missing', and RequiredEvidence appends ': a completed \u003cpayload_kind\u003e record carries one'. For a review-report this reproduces the previous message. TestMissingEvidenceSaysWhichRecordNeedsIt asserts the exact text for both record kinds, and checks errors.Is plus the evidence kind through assertEvidenceError.",
              "ExemptionRef is covered at the cheapest level. The test covers the success case, about 25 malformed or traversal refs, rejection of result and verdict refs, no output values on refusal, and errors.Is for both ErrInvalidFeature and ErrInvalidExemptionName.",
              "CheckExemptionName delegates to the existing stem helper with exemptionSuffix. It is tested against the names ExemptionName produces for n=1..12 and against a wide set of malformed names: zero, leading-zero, uppercase hex, wrong length, path, trailing whitespace and newline, and the verifier or tmp suffix variants.",
              "The added ErrInvalidExemptionName sentinel is used by CheckExemptionName and by the tests. I found no reliability regression or unproved behavior in the visible candidate."
            ]
          }
        }
